[low, doc] git-store/src/main.rs — two doc claims contradict the code. (1) Module doc (main.rs:17-19) says 'any entity ref (refs/store/<kind>/<name>) is itself a valid <tree-ish> for get/check' — true for get, false for check: check validates the resolved root tree against the schema, and the bound {value/, schema/} root is deliberately refused (the cli.rs test check_validates_a_value_tree_against_a_schema asserts exactly this); an entity ref needs the ':value' suffix. (2) document_handle's comment (main.rs:279-283) claims 'only Kind::decode and Kind::compile read/write independent of it [the kind name]' — but compile is NOT kind-independent: compile_with_schema reads the kind's schema ref (kind.rs:137). A future caller using document_handle for compile would silently compile against the schema of kind '_'. Tighten both comments.
